# Private independent-reference assets

The FDA shoulder reference has a separate, read-only delivery path. This is
groundwork for the protected review inspector, not learner admission, an
installed update, clinical approval or a registered CT/MRI overlay. The existing
learner model inventory, anatomy coverage, review source and approvals are unchanged.

The generated registry is `lib/clinical-review-reference-assets.json`. Its two
files are the exact catalogue and six-part GLB from committed Atlas
`e3a901e103e9fb495a18d9bd1622190dfc0d034b`. Catalogue revision:
`56cf325c006a00e4349a6b45844797800a11c005448d32a08f40e64664288b44`.
GLB: 8,518,472 bytes,
`38f96ede01a6cd6467fbcc4cb42eac4b673fe18c2ef54b07731e070c0968a5f6`.

## Boundaries

- Requests use `/api/atlas-delivery/references/<id>/<catalogue-sha>/models/...`.
  There is no raw/public alias, filesystem fallback, arbitrary object key or upload API.
- Every request rechecks the existing Clinical Review account/institution policy,
  including HEAD, ranges, cached conditionals and missing paths. No new role is granted.
- Registry entries are explicitly local-only. The handler additionally refuses
  non-loopback hosts. Hosted admission needs a separately authorized policy change;
  a successful local test does not provide that authority.
- Exact object key, size and stored SHA-256 are verified at both metadata and body
  reads. Responses stream with private/no-store and same-origin headers. Client-side
  source/catalogue/GLB verification remains required when the inspector is connected.
- The source frame is unitless. Anatomical axes, scale, independently confirmed
  side, bone extent, attachments and intersections remain unvalidated. Constructed
  humeral cartilage is not segmented cartilage; constructed glenoid cartilage stays held.
  Do not fit this donor into BodyParts3D or scans, enable measurements or transfer approvals.
- No patient studies, masks, identifiers, saved decisions or desktop PACS data are used.

## Reproduce in a fresh isolated checkout

Use an absolute F-drive staging package outside the Website source tree. Do not
run these commands in the owner's installed preview. Dependencies are the existing
locked Website packages; no new service or dependency is required.

```powershell
node --experimental-strip-types scripts/prepare-private-reference-assets.mjs --atlas F:/VisibleMedicine/staging/20261023-fda-review-source/atlas --output F:/VisibleMedicine/staging/NEW-private-reference-package
node --experimental-strip-types scripts/stage-private-reference-local.mjs --package F:/VisibleMedicine/staging/NEW-private-reference-package
```

The first command refuses to overwrite an existing registry/package and checks the
committed source, catalogue shape/digest and exact GLB bytes. The second refuses any
existing emulator state, uses only the isolated local FILES bucket, and verifies an
immutable write by full readback. It has no remote option or database binding.
Generated registry, objects and emulator state are local recovery material, not
cleared hosted/GitHub artifacts. See `LICENSES/PRIVATE_REFERENCE_LOCAL_ONLY.md`.

## Verification and next integration

Focused registry/guard and delivery tests, actual ephemeral workerd/R2 stream tests,
strict configured types and the stock Website build are separate evidence. Runtime
tests use a synthetic identity/DB fixture and cannot establish real signed-in routing,
institution membership changes, browser/GPU performance or clinical acceptance.
The test asks for identity encoding when checking canonical Content-Length; the first
auto-gzip header mismatch is retained, not hidden as a green first run.

Still required: import the current Atlas through the original source importer;
connect the private independent inspector and exact worksheet return identity;
bind renderer/material revisions after all Website adaptations; verify forged/stale
links, authentication/role/institution changes, unsaved navigation and actual browser
rendering together. Keep the owner's preview unchanged until new instructions.
